n":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":38,"created_at":"2026-11-05T05:13:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T05:06:57Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T05:06:34Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Part of the worlds design program: [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955). Wave-2 follow-up from the prior-art research (Lane B item 24); parent topic issue: [#5973](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5973). Research source: `workspace/scratch/worlds-capabilities-brief-2026-11-04/prior-art-research.md`.\n\n## Finding that shapes this\n\nEvery successful cross-community moderation sharing system is **data, not code**: Discord AutoMod rules are structured per-guild API objects with **no first-party import/export or cross-guild subscription** (https://docs.discord.com/developers/resources/auto-moderation); the reusable unit that actually emerged in third-party bots is a **curated feed** (cross-server network blacklists — scam domains, known raiders) plus a **policy preset** that compiles down to platform rules (Paladin: https://www.shapedimage.com/paladin-docs.html ; Azra: https://www.azrabot.com/docs/moderation.html). Reddit AutoModerator snippets are reuse-by-copy-paste — forks silently, never updates downstream; **subscription/feed beats copy-paste** for anything that must stay current. Rules-as-code packs have no successful mainstream precedent — and Garry's Mod addons (full-trust Lua, recurring malicious Workshop backdoors) are the negative evidence for executable shared moderation.\n\n## Scope\n\n#5973 designs moderation as parameterized libraries; this follow-up pins the pack as a **data format**:\n\n- Static rules (the world's own policy text).\n- Feed subscriptions (sibling feed-protocol follow-up under #5955).\n- Parameters: report threshold for auto-quarantine, moderator/reviewer set, local exemption lists — kept separate from the shared core so adopting a pack doesn't surrender local judgment (this is Drew's \"same thing, different moderators, different threshold\" as a format property).\n- Format in our manifest language (KDL profile, #5753) unless there's a reason otherwise.\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA pack-format spec (fields, versioning, parameter surface) #5973's interface design can adopt.\n","closed_by":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gis